                    {
                        "sense_id": "643156a2-ce5a-3879-b22f-e88db717d09a",
                        "entry_id": "c61547ac-d564-3294-babd-0caf50f3edc7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Something that indicates or signifies; a sign, symbol, or codeword."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fafabb54-da51-430a-9fe4-3d3a14e2a7d3",
                                "sense_id": "643156a2-ce5a-3879-b22f-e88db717d09a",
                                "text": "In other words: the advertiser creates a new sign of which the signifier consists of the happy face and the signified can be defined as \"using this product makes (you) happy\".."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e22b3922-ee83-4d82-a60a-6336ac565630",
                                "sense_id": "643156a2-ce5a-3879-b22f-e88db717d09a",
                                "text": "Hence the commitment to the primacy of the materiality of the signifier ( to shape ) is also a commitment to the primacy of experience ( to the subject position ) . Because what something looks like must be what it looks like to someone , the appeal to the shape of the signifier is at the same time an appeal to the position and hence to the identity of its interpreter."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2209853c-241f-46c9-890f-d7f1875c0353",
                                "sense_id": "643156a2-ce5a-3879-b22f-e88db717d09a",
                                "text": "Although 'corruption' is still a dominant signifier in the public realm, it has all but disappeared from the public articulations of professional associations."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
